{{!-- The Faith Received rail.

     One navigation for the library, sitting between Mere Orthodoxy's
     masthead and the page. It replaces the per-page link rows that had
     grown up surface by surface: ten links in the all-works hero, a
     different six on the research page, and nothing at all on several
     others. Ian, 2026-09-21: "Remove all other navigation that isn't
     the Mere O navbar and replace it with this rail as the primary TFR
     nav function."

     WHERE IT GOES: landing pages, the tools, and (Ian, 2026-09-23) the
     reader, where it sits above the reader's toolbar and stays pinned
     with it when the masthead scrolls away. And (Ian, 2026-09-27) the
     TFR home, above its own doors.

     Read, Research and About carry more than one destination, so they
     are buttons that open a panel rather than links that guess which
     destination you meant. Since 2026-11-11 (Ian: "make the navrail a
     mini version of the same style ... instead of the slide out, it's
     the drop downs") the panels drop below the rail in the header mega
     menu's manner: hairline columns, a title per column, a note under
     each link. The Research columns are the registry's groups and its
     notes are the registry's "what" lines. Search and Topics go straight there, because there is only
     one place to go. The brand goes to the library's front door.

     The drawer is markup, not a fetch: every destination is known at
     build time, so the rail works before any script runs and the script
     only opens and closes things. --}}
{{!-- GATED, 2026-09-22 (Ian): "if someone clicks on one anywhere in
     TFR, they should get a small subscribe form pop-up that works
     properly". Each research link carries data-feature-gate, which
     assets/js/feature-gate.js intercepts in the capture phase for anyone
     without an account: the modal opens instead of the page, and the
     link still works the moment they have one. Reading links, Scripture,
     Topics and the Dictionary carry nothing and stay open.

     Every destination in the Research drawer carries its key (2026-10-24),
     and the list of tools, their keys and their tiers is held in one
     registry, scripts/data/research-tools.json, which
     scripts/check-research-tools.mjs compares with this file.

     The tier these resolve to lives in ONE place, feature-gate.js's
     TFR_BETA_OPEN_TO_ALL_MEMBERS, checked against both library workers
